      },
      "lineNbr": 111,
      "author": {
        "id": 1682499
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-16T19:57:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, correct. But using singleton comes with all related \"benefits\": extra logic for lazy initialization, synchronization and making both manual and unit testing more complex. The method is not used too often, so I do not think there\u0027s much value in caching the filter.\n\nDo you have any major concerns keeping it as is?",
      "parentUuid": "f4ec7517_967e0c31",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 111,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 111,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "c961228e0c49af2dfc672c098faf7453da2eff08",
